@startuml signed-ingress
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

title Signed ingress: bridge, trust gate, injection, journal, projection

actor "Operator or peer" as OP $PERSON
participant "Bridge inbox\n(binding)" as BR $CARRIER
participant "Ingress trust gate" as TG $SERVICE
participant "curator-trust\n+ mandates" as TR $PRIVATE
participant "Durable command queue" as CQ $PRIVATE
participant "Supervisor" as SU $SERVICE
participant "Harness adapter" as AD $SERVICE
participant "Holder" as HO $SERVICE
participant "Harness" as NA $AGENT
database "Event journal" as JO $COMMITTED
participant "Projection +\nconsumer" as PR $CARRIER

== Admit ==
OP -> BR: signed envelope
BR -> TG: frozen bytes + binding
TG -> TR: verify signature, resolve pin,\ncheck grant, freshness/replay
TR --> TG: admitted / refused

alt refused
  TG --> BR: rejection + reason code
  BR --> OP: rejection (nothing reaches the model)
else admitted
  TG -> TG: deterministic checks,\nframing, atomic commit
  TG -> CQ: durable command + evidence
end

== Inject (admitted only) ==
CQ -> SU: next command\n(reauthorize at dispatch)
SU -> AD: typed write at a turn boundary
AD -> HO: authenticated write\n(identity, epoch, generation, lease)
HO -> NA: structured surface\n(stream-json, app-server, MSP)
note right of HO
  PTY only through the holder.
  Never tmux.
end note

== Observe ==
NA --> HO: structured events
HO --> AD: events
AD --> JO: normalized events
JO --> PR: snapshot + tail\n(audience-checked)
PR --> OP: state and pending decisions

caption Sources: Architecture v1 §A3, §A4, §A5; session-core study rev 3
@enduml
